From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Prithwiraj Samanta <prskid1000@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 09:55:08 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] common : add defer_loading and tool_reference to tool
 definitions

A tool with defer_loading stays in the sampling grammar but its schema is
left out of the rendered prompt, so a client can keep a large tool set
callable without paying for every schema in context, and without
invalidating the prompt cache when a tool is revealed later.

Templates that handle the flag themselves (GLM-5.x) are detected with a
caps probe and get the full tool list with the flag set; for other
templates the deferred tools are removed before rendering. All tools may
be deferred only when the template handles the flag.

A tool message made of {"type": "tool_reference", "tool_name"|"name": X}
parts reveals a deferred tool. Templates that expand references (GLM-5.3)
get them as is (second caps probe); for others each reference is replaced
with the tool definition as JSON text. A reference to an undeclared tool
is an error. The Anthropic /v1/messages conversion passes defer_loading
and tool_reference through.

Ref: #28179

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
